  "note": "The x/(4φ(q)) term is the odd-m constant of (5.54); for all m it is x/(2φ(q)). Lean needs W ≥ 50000, and its (2.19)-type bound (1/2)W log W now holds for W ≥ 2·10⁶ rather than the book's W ≥ 117."
